arked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to seal himself and a thousand courtiers within a fortified, elaborately designed abbey to escape the contagion. Months later, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored rooms, each with stained-glass windows matching their hue, culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting the festivities and instilling dread. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death—cloaked in grave-cloths and smeared with blood—appears, moving silently through the rooms; the prince, enraged by the blasphemy, pursues the figure with a dagger, but the intruder turns in the black chamber, and the prince collapses dead upon contact. The revelers, overcome with terror, seize the figure only to find it empty, revealing the Red Death itself has infiltrated the abbey, and one by one, all the guests die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_mummer_e8d085c7\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the mummer\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 3,\n      \"confidenc