        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...his group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which t...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: adj (di-LIB-er-it); verb (di-LIB-er-ayt)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"glossary\": null,\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"structure\": {\n      \"chapter_count\": 1,\n      \"has_titles\": false,\n      \"has_parts\": false,\n      \"narrative_style\": \"unknown\",\n      \"description\": \"This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.\"\n    },\n    \"plot_summary\": {\n      \"plot_summary\": \"In the face of a merciless plague known as the Red Death—characterized by bleeding from the pores and swift, agonizing death—Prince Prospero retreats with a thousand courtiers into a secluded, heavily fortified abbey, seeking refuge from the devastation ravaging the outside world. The abbey, a marvel of opulence and design, is divided into seven uniquely colored chambers, each adorned with stained-glass windows that cast vivid hues across the floor. At its heart lies a black chamber, its walls draped in ebony, its windows blood-red, and dominated by a massive, ominous clock that chimes each hour, halting all revelry and plunging the guests into silent dread. Prospero, a man of extravagant tastes and self-imposed isolation, hosts a lavish masked ball to distract from the grim reality beyond the abbey’s walls, indulging in music, dance, and illusion as a defiant act against mortality.\\n\\nAs the night unfolds, the festivities grow increasingly frenzied, yet the hourly chime of the ebony clock continues to disrupt the revelry, each toll a chilling reminder of time’s inexorable march. Then, at midnight, a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, draped in grave-cloths and smeared with blood, moving silently through the rooms. The guests are horrified, but the prince, consumed by fury at the blasphemy of such a mockery, draws a dagger and pursues the intruder through the chambers. The figure leads him into the black chamber, where, upon confrontation, the prince collapses dead, his life extinguished in an instant. The revelers, now paralyzed by terror, rush to seize the figure, only to discover it is hollow—empty, like a shell—revealing that the Red Death has not merely been imitated, but has infiltrated the abbey in physical form.\\n\\nThe realization strikes with devastating clarity: the plague has breached the sanctuary, and the prince’s arrogance and denial of death have invited the very fate he sought to escape. One by one, the guests fall, succumbing to the Red Death as the clock chimes its final hour and the lights go out. Darkness consumes the abbey, and with it, all life within. The story ends not with triumph or redemption, but with the inevitable triumph of death over human defiance, underscoring the futility of attempting to outwit fate through wealth, isolation, or spectacle. The narrative concludes with the chilling silence of a world where no one remains to witness the end.\\n\\n\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"identity\",\n        \"ambition\",\n        \"loss\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruc